  "summary": "Tracing the schematic against the specification, every functional element the spec describes as actually implemented is present and correctly valued: the two MCP2515 CAN controllers use 16 MHz crystals (Y1/Y3, matching the '16mhz not 12mhz' correction), the isolated CAN transceivers and SM712-family CAN TVS arrays are in place, the LTC4412+P-FET ideal-diode USB OR-ing circuit (U32/Q13) exists, the e-stop buffers and per-branch indicator LEDs match the July-10 changelog, and the camera pins are left unconnected as the notes call for. The apparent mismatches (U6 being an LDO rather than the LTC4412, U8/U9/U11 being the IMU/ESD/USB-UART rather than the CAN parts, the RTC being absent) are reference-designator renumberings between the spec's reference netlist and this build, plus the documented open/pointer items (RTC link, GLOBAL_EN sequencing, CAN-LED polarity) that the spec explicitly says are not anomalies. I found no drawing-supported deviation that would change the board's behaviour."
}

